WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:07.027
What's up guys, we're Pongfinity!

00:00:07.027 --> 00:00:08.792
Today we're practising with Benedek Olah.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.553
Let's have a good practise!
Come on!

00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:24.068
So before you come to the practise

00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:26.856
it's important to set your mind already
what you're going to do.

00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:29.288
Like you have to know when is your tournament

00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:30.703
or when is your next match.

00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:31.942
If you play in the weekends,

00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:34.460
Mondays you can push it a little bit harder with the footworks.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.036
So today is kind of footwork and strength training

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:40.583
and I like to do some small stuff which I have problems in the match

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:42.374
so I can also correct my mistakes.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:45.192
But before the practise starts, I know what I'm going to do.

00:01:18.322 --> 00:01:19.585
Exersice one.

00:01:19.585 --> 00:01:22.894
In this exercise players play backhand topspin against each other

00:01:22.894 --> 00:01:26.418
with high speed and whenever Miikka wants to change here

00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:29.211
I'll try to catch it with a fast controlled forehand drive.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:34.511
This excersice is good to develop your reaction speed from the backhand side

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:37.374
and also gives you a steady safe feeling in the backhand.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:41.900
Remember to keep your racket always up so you can keep up with the speed here.

00:01:43.416 --> 00:01:44.278
Exercise two.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:48.977
Here we have Miikka play forehand loop from the middle for me all over the table.

00:01:51.522 --> 00:01:55.856
It's hard excercise for both of you so try to keep up the good quality

00:01:55.856 --> 00:01:58.069
and hit as many as you can on the table.

00:01:58.513 --> 00:02:00.096
This is also super fun to play!

00:02:01.176 --> 00:02:03.176
I can't do anything from that!

00:02:04.867 --> 00:02:07.329
Excercise 3: Forehand tactical counter loop.

00:02:09.427 --> 00:02:13.718
Here we work on our forehand finishing shot with an optional backhand finish.

00:02:13.718 --> 00:02:18.414
We give one side a half-long service, which he opens up to our forehand side

00:02:18.414 --> 00:02:20.500
and we work on finishing the point here.

00:02:21.987 --> 00:02:25.282
It's important to do this from your match services also

00:02:25.282 --> 00:02:27.911
to get used to the spins you get from your own service.

00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:30.566
Critical jackpot!

00:02:32.148 --> 00:02:35.581
Excercise 4: This is all about small detail spins

00:02:35.581 --> 00:02:37.789
and how you continue the game after that.

00:02:39.137 --> 00:02:42.143
This is very tactical and various for every person.

00:02:42.843 --> 00:02:45.740
Try to picture how people normally return your service

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.551
and how you will make a point from that.

00:02:50.055 --> 00:02:52.650
Multiball, here we can practise most effectively

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.618
because your partner shouldn't miss any balls.

00:02:56.581 --> 00:02:57.757
One-two, one-two, one-two.

00:02:58.532 --> 00:03:01.863
First one short, one long underspin after that.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.820
Middle middle, backhand backhand, straight lines.

00:03:08.799 --> 00:03:10.401
So I flip, and you give me...
Yes!

00:03:10.401 --> 00:03:13.410
Then the next one short and one long topspin.

00:03:14.718 --> 00:03:17.279
Here we develop the in and out movement.

00:03:17.642 --> 00:03:20.783
Your multiball partner will not give you time between the two balls

00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:24.784
and you have to move back after the short like your life depends on it!

00:03:26.702 --> 00:03:27.546
Change, let's go!

00:03:28.515 --> 00:03:30.515
Short long, extremely fast like, one-two.

00:03:31.513 --> 00:03:34.401
Important to make the short return with good quality

00:03:34.401 --> 00:03:37.271
not just giving a high ball with not so much spin.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:41.843
You play here or here, tatatatataa.

00:03:41.843 --> 00:03:42.847
Excercise two:

00:03:44.333 --> 00:03:46.333
Fast tempo balls all over the table.

00:03:48.886 --> 00:03:49.386
Faster!

00:03:50.217 --> 00:03:53.349
This needs some skill from the coach too because it's so fast.

00:03:55.203 --> 00:03:57.203
So you have to keep your hand always up,

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.274
otherwise you're going to be late.

00:04:00.633 --> 00:04:06.183
It's all about reaction speed and hitting the ball
 as quicky as possible without mistakes.

00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:09.959
If you miss too many, you should try to put some balls on the table first

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:12.380
before advancing to the higher level and speed.

00:04:13.047 --> 00:04:14.658
So idea now is the cross-step.

00:04:14.658 --> 00:04:17.011
And the point is when you make the cross-step,

00:04:17.011 --> 00:04:18.435
you go forward with it.

00:04:18.842 --> 00:04:20.362
So that it's not a defensive one.

00:04:20.762 --> 00:04:24.265
Now this will be though on the legs and is also something I'm not so good at.

00:04:24.265 --> 00:04:29.015
You try to move to the forehand with one cross-leg-step as far as you can go

00:04:29.015 --> 00:04:32.215
and come back from this position and continue the game.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.855
One more you can do it!
Come on put everything there!

00:04:40.896 --> 00:04:42.153
Jump, jump!

00:04:44.845 --> 00:04:45.441
Otto your turn.

00:04:47.275 --> 00:04:48.254
Oh my god!

00:04:49.106 --> 00:04:52.057
You should use cross-step when you have to cover a lot of ground

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:54.569
and a single normal step is not enough.

00:05:06.101 --> 00:05:10.094
Allright so hope you guys enjoyed seeing
 how an olympic table tennis player practises.

00:05:10.592 --> 00:05:13.636
Don't forget to subscribe right here, until next time!

